@startuml
title How a label becomes a spot on the curve
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
  StartColor #4A78B5
  EndColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F7FAFF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}

start
:Take the label,\nfor example "ALICE WINS";
:Run it through a scrambler\nto get one huge number;

note right
  The scrambler always gives the
  same number for the same label,
  but you cannot work backwards
  from the number to the label.
end note

repeat
  :Add 1 to the number;
  :Ask: is there a spot on the\ncurved line at this number?;
repeat while (Found a spot?) is (no, try the next number) not (yes)
->yes;

:Pick the top or bottom spot\n(the scrambler decides which);
#EEF5FF:This spot is the sticker's name;

note right
  About half of all numbers land on
  the curve, so this usually takes
  one or two tries.
end note

if (Is this sticker built on top\nof another sticker?) then (yes)
  :Add the two spots together\nusing the curve's adding rule;
  :The answer is another spot,\nand that is the combined name;
else (no)
endif

stop
@enduml
